{
	"_units": "Combined arms A2 (docs/combined_arms.md 2.2, 2.3.5; cg_brief queue item 2.1): the internal modules of each armoured model, merged into the model's spec by VehicleSpecs.spec and read by VehicleModules. A model with \"modules\" here takes its damage on them; one without (technicals, aircraft, static weapons) keeps its old hit zones (data/vehicles.json \"zones\"), and VehicleModules.layout builds its modules from those zones so every model has a layout to read. box: [x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1] in the vehicle frame (front is -z), as zones and plates. kind: what damage does (kinds below and 2.2.2). hp: in the hp_kj units shells' module_dmg uses (0: an air volume that takes no damage). absorb_mm: mm of a round's residual penetration the module eats as the round crosses it (a shaped charge's jet x1.5 after the first module). zone: which of the old hit zones it answers for (Vehicle.zone_health; hull is the structure). fire: [chance on a KE penetration through it, on a CE one]. external: outside the armour (an outside HE burst reaches it). seat: a crew module's seat (its box is the seated body's unless given); seats not named here are riders (troop). gun_seat: the armament module of that gun seat (destroyed: the seat can't fire). rounds / detonate [KE pen, CE pen, HE inside] / on_detonate (vent: blow-out panels, the crew unhurt; cook_off: rounds burn off, a fire; catastrophic: the vehicle goes up): ammo stowage (2.10.2). spall_liner and belly come from data/vehicle_armour.json. Every number is Proposed, from docs/combined_arms.md 2.2.3 and public layouts.",
